    </font></b><br>
    <font size="2"> <i>Mention greenhouse gas (GHG) today and you conjure
up images of shrinking polar ice caps, rising oceans, depleted rain
forests, expanding deserts and even rising crime rates. Although there is
still much dissension among the ranks of scientists and environmentalists
as to the impact GHG has on the environment, there can be little doubt the
earth&#39;s climate is predicted to change because human activities are
altering the chemical composition of the atmosphere through the buildup of
greenhouse gases ? primarily carbon dioxide, methane, and nitrous
oxide.</i><br>
    <br>
    The heat-trapping property of these gases is undisputed. Although
uncertainty exists about exactly how earth&#39;s climate responds to these
gases, global temperatures are rising. In recognition of the role
greenhouse gas plays in global warming and climatic change,
representatives of more than... <a
